Michael A. Smith wrote:
> It has "Intergraph Computer Systems" written all over it
>   [Intergraph has a inpenetrable website]

Intergraph produces CAD software.  On the hardware side, they used to
produce their own unix worstations (based on the Clipper CPU, incomaptible
with everything).  Years ago, they switched their hardware focus to the
NT market, and now sell NT workstations with some spiffed-up hardware.
Sounds like you have one of their high-end 3D cards (of course, I don't
know how old it is...).  I don't think Intergraph gives out hardware specs
though, so it's probably only usable under NT.

-Mitch


