> The cost to consumer is not twice, not thrice, but at least 5 times
> their build cost.  One heck of a profit, but I wonder how long Q
> can keep up that game with folks like API and other ISVs in the
> market?

That's an interesting thought.  Conspiracy theories are always good
fodder to get the masses riled up.  Of course, it would be even more
interesting if it had some basis in fact.  Do you have real world cost
figures to back up your assertion?  If the cost figures are real, can 
you get me a list of the suppliers?  I'd like to buy my parts at the
